Spoilers:

>I beleive you can only write spellbooks of a type you have already read, and
>spellbook types don't correspond to scroll types.  I've found that writing
>spellbooks will run all but the the most fully charged marker dry, and leave
>you with nothing; I think you're better off saving them for scrolls.  I also,
>if I have ID'd them already, make it a point to write a scroll of charging
>first, especially if I can make it blessed.  You can only charge a marker once,
>but it's worth it.

There's a small chance, miniscule unless you're a wizard, of successfully
writing a scroll/spellbook that you haven't seen before.  While it's true
that spellbooks take a lot more charges out of your marker than scrolls,
that blessed spellbook of identify or magic mapping goes a lot further
than a single scroll, and leaves you with a blank spellbook to be 
rewritten when you're done.  If you have multiple markers (polypiling
helps) then it's worth using up a couple this way.

